// AirTAK Android — ui/help/HelpContent.kt
//
// Issue #11: this file used to carry the entire in-app guide as ~150 Kotlin string
// literals, which made the guide the one part of the app that could not be translated at
// all — the German build showed English help next to German buttons.
//
// The text now lives in res/values/help.xml and res/values-de/help.xml, generated by
// tools/i18n_help.py. This file keeps the structure (topic → intro → entries) and reads
// the words from resources, so the guide follows the system or in-app language like
// every other screen.
//
// Keys are positional (`help_t3_e5_body`) because the guide has no natural ids and the
// key order is the on-screen order. Add a topic by adding its keys in both locales and
// bumping TOPIC_COUNT / ENTRY_COUNTS; `tools/i18n_help.py … check` fails if the two
// locales disagree.

package com.airtak.ui.help

import androidx.compose.runtime.Composable
import androidx.compose.ui.res.stringResource
import com.airtak.R

